+			<p>“<abbr epub:type="z3998:name-title">Mrs.</abbr> <abbr epub:type="z3998:surname">M.</abbr> has made her plans, I dare say, and will play her cards well, early as it is. The girl evidently doesn’t think of it yet,” said <abbr epub:type="z3998:name-title">Mrs.</abbr> Moffat.</p>
 			<p>“She told that fib about her mamma, as if she did know, and colored up when the flowers came, quite prettily. Poor thing! she’d be so nice if she was only got up in style. Do you think she’d be offended if we offered to lend her a dress for Thursday?” asked another voice.</p>
 			<p>“She’s proud, but I don’t believe she’d mind, for that dowdy tarlatan is all she has got. She may tear it tonight, and that will be a good excuse for offering a decent one.”</p>
 			<p>“We’ll see. I shall ask young Laurence, as a compliment to her, and we’ll have fun about it afterward.”</p>
